import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"dsh analysis, Rho results and a selected-row question","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/dsh-rho-episode.md","filePath":"records/dsh-rho-episode.md"}'),i={name:"records/dsh-rho-episode.md"};function n(r,e,d,l,h,c){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="dsh-analysis-rho-results-and-a-selected-row-question" tabindex="-1">dsh analysis, Rho results and a selected-row question <a class="header-anchor" href="#dsh-analysis-rho-results-and-a-selected-row-question" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;dsh analysis, Rho results and a selected-row question&quot;">​</a></h1><p>2026-10-31 local / 2026-11-01 UTC. This episode implements the requested <code>dsh-rho</code> prototype: analyse in dsh, show the outputs with existing Rho components, select a result and continue the original conversation. It follows the native plugin example in <a href="https://github.com/bowenliang123/dsh-context" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">dsh-context</a> and the installed dsh 0.2.1-rc.5 public APIs. The result is a local package, not a published npm or signed distribution.</p><h2 id="what-was-built" tabindex="-1">What was built <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-was-built" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What was built&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The application adapter lives in <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/../adapters/dsh-rho/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">adapters/dsh-rho</a>. Its Cordis host registers <code>rho_present</code> and an authenticated result-reading route; its browser entry contributes <strong>Rho</strong> to dsh&#39;s <code>conversation.view</code> slot. Native session identity supplies both the tool&#39;s caller and the view&#39;s result scope. dsh owns analysis, permissions, tools, model and history. It is not started as a second Agent inside Rho.</p><p>The selected owners are Files 0.5.0, Tables 0.5.0, Media 0.4.0 and Contracts 0.4.0 from Rho-plugins commit <code>1173789010e4679180804aa309e661b218198f70</code>. Their public APIs, TableView and MediaView are consumed unchanged. The adapter supplies composition, session archives and a transient selection port; it reuses Rho&#39;s existing POSIX writer lease. No Core or Rho-plugins source changed, and neither the Core Host nor the Rho backend is started.</p><p><code>rho_present</code> captures completed project files. CSV columns and types are explicit; row selection needs a unique string key. Questions resolve those keys against the captured version, then use dsh&#39;s native revision-checked draft insertion and normal Send action. A question can be read or revised before sending. Closing the view, reading a result and reconnecting do not execute analysis.</p><h2 id="real-episode-and-observations" tabindex="-1">Real episode and observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#real-episode-and-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Real episode and observations&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The owned fixture used a disposable project and isolated <code>DSH_HOME</code>, dsh 0.2.1-rc.5, Node 22.22.3, Python 3 and headless Google Chrome on macOS. It used the existing configured gateway with <code>westlakehpc/deepseek-v4.1-flash</code>; credentials were read in memory and not put in source, patches or evidence. The person&#39;s running Desktop Harness and projects were not restarted.</p><p>The six input values were alpha: 1, 2, 8 and beta: -3, 4, 7. A single native prompt asked dsh to write and run a standard-library Python analysis once, append one run marker, emit a CSV and SVG, and present both with <code>rho_present</code>. The model wrote <code>analysis.py</code>, ran it and presented both outputs. The run took 3 minutes 32 seconds.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Observations</th><th>Mean in retained CSV</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>alpha</td><td>3</td><td>3.6666666666666665</td></tr><tr><td>beta</td><td>3</td><td>2.6666666666666665</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The browser showed both rows and the labelled two-bar figure. Selecting alpha changed the question label to <strong>Ask about 1 selected row</strong>. A Chinese question asked for its group, count and mean and whether this was the overall mean. The pre-existing draft <code>请用中文回答。</code> survived insertion. The added context contained only alpha, its exact numeric values, original path, snapshot digest, capture time and the same session ID. Sent once through the native composer, the model answered in 13 seconds: alpha, n = 3, mean approximately 3.67; this was alpha&#39;s mean and did not establish the combined mean. It ran no analysis for the question.</p><p>Retained identities:</p><ul><li>Session: <code>session-38a2a4c4-1e62-46f3-8ff6-234d7d098ca7</code>.</li><li>CSV tool call: <code>chatcmpl-tool-a6473a9aeace26b0</code>; SHA-256 <code>e2bba75703875eb8484e302157f29d28a42705fa3b21332897bf86f87ba31017</code>.</li><li>SVG tool call: <code>chatcmpl-tool-a9ee726ca0c532ff</code>; SHA-256 <code>1cb9430aed9b827880f63b866e539215b2daeab70926119ff4dfb22f9a027cb0</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="failures-that-changed-the-implementation" tabindex="-1">Failures that changed the implementation <a class="header-anchor" href="#failures-that-changed-the-implementation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Failures that changed the implementation&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Loading an absolute package directory as a host module failed with an ESM directory import error. The source fixture now resolves the package by name; delivery uses an ordinary tarball installed by <code>dsh plugin</code>.</li><li>The first model session used dsh&#39;s retained default workspace instead of the disposable folder. It found no input and did no analysis. The fixture now explicitly creates/selects its workspace with dsh&#39;s public controller. The installation instructions require choosing the matching folder in dsh.</li><li>Comparing the browser Origin with the handler&#39;s internal request URL rejected valid result reads. dsh uses a carrier-neutral internal URL. The adapter now relies on the connection service&#39;s authenticated <code>/api</code> boundary and retains the cross-site refusal; it still validates original session and project scope.</li><li>Files&#39; captured resources name archive paths. Routing those paths back into the analysis project made four initial store checks fail. The adapter&#39;s path provider now resolves captured internal paths in its archive and ordinary paths through Files&#39; project containment. All five store checks then passed.</li><li>An exclusive lock file survived the first owned-host shutdown. Reusing Rho&#39;s kernel-held writer lease removed stale-unlink/PID-reuse recovery. A second writer is refused, and the installed plugin reopened the same archive after both normal shutdown and an abrupt kill of its owned dsh process.</li></ol><p>A browser assertion initially read an empty draft before asynchronous insertion completed. Waiting for the native Chat view switch resolved the observation; the same captured values were then verified. No analysis prompt was resent. Package assembly also caught nested AG Grid package metadata without adjacent licenses; notices now come from each actual bundled dependency root, including <code>ag-stack</code>. An installation-guide dry run also showed that <code>npm --prefix ... pack</code> selected the root application. The verified command now names <code>npm pack ./adapters/dsh-rho</code>.</p><h2 id="verification-and-installation" tabindex="-1">Verification and installation <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-and-installation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification and installation&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>npm run build</code>, five store tests and a TypeScript check over the adapter&#39;s three source files passed. The tests cover snapshot overwrite/reopen, original-call retries, scope/path/key rejection, budgets and competing writers. They do not claim full Rho application acceptance; its unrelated suite was not run.</p><p>In the real browser:</p><ul><li>Table and SVG views, row selection, the existing Chinese draft and same-session model continuation all worked. Screens were inspected at 1440, 768 and 390 px; narrow results use scrolling. No browser page errors were recorded.</li><li>Offline result reads showed an error and <strong>Try again</strong> while keeping displayed results. Restoring the connection recovered those same results.</li><li>Editing the chat draft while a delayed question request was pending refused insertion and kept <code>Newer draft ✓</code> intact.</li><li>Refresh and a normal owned-host restart restored the original conversation and both results. The test then installed the tarball through <code>dsh plugin --profile web add &lt;tarball&gt; --ignore-scripts --offline</code>, which added and enabled its bundle. Its archive and draft insertion worked after launch.</li><li>Overwriting the original CSV with alpha mean 999 did not alter the displayed snapshot or the selected-row question, which still carried 3.6666666666666665. The test restored the original CSV afterward.</li><li>After an abrupt owned-host process kill, the installed package reopened the archive and original session without removing the lock file. At the end, <code>run-count.txt</code> still had exactly one line and the archive still had two results.</li></ul><p>Local evidence is under <code>work/dsh-rho/prototype-03/</code>: <code>evidence.json</code>, <code>chat.txt</code>, the native question drafts, original CSV, screenshots of empty/results/selection/ answer/failure/recovery/narrow states, and <code>dsh-rho-0.0.1.tgz</code>. The private launch address stays outside the repository. The fixture and native session history are retained in the disposable <code>/tmp/rho-dsh-prototype-03</code> directory. The package&#39;s composition manifest records exact bundle inputs and selected local overrides; it is not an official release attestation.</p><p>The delivered package is <code>work/dsh-rho/package/dsh-rho-0.0.1.tgz</code>, SHA-256 <code>4ffe8b2798d2d0ead6e558f9d26599bd63b1d5d0b7eecd54efa85684e5396266</code>. Final review keyed result choices and questions by original tool call as well as snapshot, so two presentations of identical bytes retain their own titles. The five tests and strict type check passed; the final tarball was installed again, and its table, figure, native draft insertion and original call ID were checked in the same session without resending analysis. The run count remained one.</p><h2 id="what-this-establishes-and-what-remains" tabindex="-1">What this establishes and what remains <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-establishes-and-what-remains" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What this establishes and what remains&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This observed episode establishes the requested local loop with reused components and one native dsh conversation. The adapter is deliberately one-project and one selected dsh release candidate. It has no general Studio, notebook, live variable inspection or automatic output discovery. Row selections are transient, image questions carry references rather than pixels, and a question&#39;s structured context is visible in the native draft. React comes from Harness; broader compatibility with the components&#39; declared React peer version is not established by this run.</p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/../adapters/dsh-rho/README.md#ownership-and-limits" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">package README</a> names the budgets, configuration and refusal behavior. Invalid table content can leave a bounded captured file unlisted. There is no silent deletion of earlier results or automatic replay of unknown work. Independent researcher use, Desktop/TUI entry points, Windows locking and public package distribution remain untested.</p>',26)])])}const b=t(i,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,b as default};
